filter: a disposed focus window gets no wait cursor

The PDF and SVG exports put a wait cursor on Application's focus window.
That window can be one already disposed: vcl keeps it as the focus
while a closed view's frame goes (ImplNewInputContext checks for this),
and dispose() frees its WindowImpl. AddEventListener and EnterWait then
dereference null. Ely saw it on macOS, where the worker runs the Cocoa
backend: a mail merge closed one document, opened another and exported
it as PDF; the worker died with SIGSEGV in PDFFilter::filter (1 run in
10 of the release tests under load).
Both exports now skip a disposed focus window and warn.
--- a/filter/source/pdf/pdffilter.cxx
+++ b/filter/source/pdf/pdffilter.cxx
@@ -17,6 +17,7 @@
  *   the License at http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0 .
  */
 
+#include <ely/log.hxx>
 #include "pdffilter.hxx"
 #include "pdfexport.hxx"
 #include <cppuhelper/supportsservice.hxx>
@@ -210,6 +211,12 @@
     FocusWindowWaitCursor() :
         m_pFocusWindow( Application::GetFocusWindow() )
     {
+        // Ely: a closed view's window can keep the focus.
+        if (m_pFocusWindow && m_pFocusWindow->isDisposed())
+        {
+            ELY_WARN("ely.filter", "the focus window is disposed; no wait cursor");
+            m_pFocusWindow.reset();
+        }
         if( m_pFocusWindow )
         {
             m_pFocusWindow->AddEventListener( LINK( this, FocusWindowWaitCursor, DestroyedLink ) );
